---
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#e9e2d2" />
    <title>Verse Lens — Itihāsa Atlas</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="subpage verse-page">
      <header class="subnav">
        <a class="wordmark wordmark--ink" href="/">
          ITIHĀSA <span>ATLAS</span>
        </a>
        <nav aria-label="Product navigation">
          <a href="/#atlas">ATLAS</a>
          <a aria-current="page" href="/verse-lens">
            VERSE LENS
          </a>
          <a href="/pathfinder">PATHFINDER</a>
          <a href="/protocol">PROTOCOL</a>
        </nav>
      </header>

      <section class="verse-hero" data-od-id="verse-entry">
        <div>
          <p class="label">VERSE LENS / DRAFT READING 001</p>
          <p class="verse-hero__eyebrow">BHAGAVAD GĪTĀ 1.1</p>
          <h1>Before the first answer, there is a question.</h1>
        </div>
        <p class="verse-hero__deck">
          A lens for slowing down at a verse: its sound, its construction and the
          editorial limits of any English rendering.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="verse-plate" data-od-id="verse-plate">
        <div class="verse-plate__folio">FOLIO 01 / CRITICAL EDITION BASELINE</div>
        <p class="verse-plate__sanskrit">धर्मक्षेत्रे कुरुक्षेत्रे समवेता युयुत्सवः ।</p>
        <p class="verse-plate__sanskrit">मामकाः पाण्डवाश्चैव किमकुर्वत सञ्जय ॥</p>
        <div class="verse-plate__grid">
          <p>
            <span>dharmakṣetre</span> in the field named for dharma
          </p>
          <p>
            <span>kurukṣetre</span> in the field of the Kurus
          </p>
          <p>
            <span>samavetāḥ</span> having assembled together
          </p>
          <p>
            <span>yuyutsavaḥ</span> desiring to fight
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="verse-note" data-od-id="verse-note">
        <p class="label">READING NOTE</p>
        <blockquote>
          The verse frames a battlefield twice: as Kuru territory and as a dharma-field.
          That double naming is not a conclusion. It is the pressure under every
          conclusion that follows.
        </blockquote>
        <div>
          <p>
            This is a study gloss, not a published translation. The Sanskrit text and
            every word note require edition and reviewer verification before publication.
          </p>
          <a href="/verses/gita">OPEN SOURCE RECORD ↗</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
